<article class="env-definition" id="09CA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09CA">Definition <span data-tag="09CA">10.59.6</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $M$ be a finite $R$-module. The <em>Hilbert polynomial</em> of $M$ over $R$ is the element $P(t) \in \mathbf{Q}[t]$ such that $P(n) = \varphi _ M(n)$ for $n \gg 0$. </p>
